| The bitbucket server (#2828): our tools and events — pull requests, their checks (commit statuses: Pipelines or any CI) and issues — on Bitbucket Cloud's REST API 2.0, with the Bitbucket connection (#3785) or `BITBUCKET_TOKEN` (an Atlassian API token with `BITBUCKET_EMAIL`, or an access token); Cloud only, not Data Center; views (#3866): Pull requests, Issues and a pull request's page | agents | built, tested with a fake Bitbucket | Tools, Events, Views, Workflows | 2026-11-06, against a fake Bitbucket over HTTP (`Go/internal/bitbucketmcp/*_test.go`): every event (trust by the repository's permissions or the workspace's members, forks, apps and bots, drafts, conflicts from the diffstat, merge and decline times from the activity, an issue tracker that is off, the cursor), `failed_log` (failed steps, a Range of the log's end from a file store on another host, without the token), `retry_pipeline` (a new run with the old run's target and variables, refusing a run not ended or with a secured variable), `run.completed` for a Pipelines run of any trigger, with its successful deployments as `deploys` (#4217), the errors as the events draft's codes, the remotes, and the tools through the front. 2026-11-07, the views (#3866) against a fake Bitbucket over HTTP (`Go/internal/bitbucketmcp/views_test.go`), then pinned in a scratch app against a fake Bitbucket (`Web/test/walk/bitbucket3866-fake.py`) and walked on the web page in headless Chrome (`Web/test/walk/bitbucket3866.mjs`, 15 checks: sections, a pull request's tabs, a failed run's log, Merge asked again, the app's diff, an issue's description and Start Agent), and drawn in the Mac window. 2026-11-07, lineage (#3879) against a fake Bitbucket over HTTP (`Go/internal/bitbucketmcp/lineage_test.go`: a node's title and state, a release's commits over two pages, a commit's pull request, the cost comment posted, edited and posted again) and in the host (`Go/internal/agentsd/lineagebitbucket_test.go`) | `Go/cmd/bitbucket-mcp/main.go`, `Go/internal/bitbucketmcp` | not yet on a real workspace (Alex's test, #3771): Bitbucket Cloud has no local container; issues have no labels, so an issue's kind and component stand in; the views' sidebar rows only for a project's other repository (the Work pages list the folder's own since #3786); lineage's reads (`/commit/<ref>`, `/commits?include=&exclude=`, `/commit/<sha>/pullrequests`, which needs the repository's commit links) and the cost comment's `PUT` are unproven on a real account; `failed_log` (#3787) reads a Pipelines run by its build number and a step's log with a Range, unproven on a real account; `retry_pipeline` (#3792) starts a new run (Pipelines has no rerun of the failed steps), and its target's fields, read back from a run, are unproven on a real account; checks and conflicts read for the 50 open pull requests updated last; `run.completed` (#4217) reads the completed runs created in the 12 hours before a poll and a run's deploys from the newest 50 deployments, unproven on a real account; no `deploy.waiting`: Bitbucket has no API for a deploy that waits; `deploy.started`, `deploy.succeeded` and `deploy.failed` (#5244) tested with a fake only, not yet on a real account |
